WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.980
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.250 --> 00:03.710
He really looks exactly like him.

3
00:03.710 --> 00:05.250
But they're nothing alike.

4
00:05.250 --> 00:06.810
I'm such a fool.

5
00:06.810 --> 00:10.520
Of course Master Seki wouldn't be here.

6
00:11.340 --> 00:13.160
I want to go home.

7
00:15.250 --> 00:17.090
I want to go home.

8
00:25.820 --> 00:27.870
What are you doing?

9
00:29.220 --> 00:32.840
Ms. Nashiki?

10
00:33.870 --> 00:37.220
What were you doing just now?

11
00:38.800 --> 00:40.900
No, there's been a misunderstanding!

12
00:40.900 --> 00:42.200
Please, listen to me!

13
00:42.200 --> 00:43.930
Ms. Nashiki!

14
00:49.880 --> 00:51.110
I'm so sorry!

15
00:51.110 --> 00:54.030
I didn't mean to!

16
00:58.530 --> 01:06.590
[Music Room (2)]

17
01:12.400 --> 01:13.970
Ms. Nashiki!

18
01:13.970 --> 01:16.800
You came to watch today?

19
01:16.800 --> 01:18.650
You seemed busy recently.

20
01:18.650 --> 01:21.930
We all saw you practicing for the Sports Festival, Ms. Nashiki.

21
01:21.930 --> 01:25.160
You were running so weird!

22
01:25.160 --> 01:28.160
I saw her asking the lunch ladies how they made their curry.

23
01:28.160 --> 01:30.370
- What? - Me too! That was hilarious!

24
01:30.370 --> 01:32.740
Why did you ask?

25
01:32.740 --> 01:34.780
It's just curry!

26
01:37.520 --> 01:40.580
Ms. Nashiki?

27
01:41.490 --> 01:43.990
- May 13th... - Are you okay?

28
01:45.770 --> 01:46.980
Is that today?

29
01:46.980 --> 01:50.060
- Yeah. - It is.

30
01:58.510 --> 02:01.180
- Ms. Nashiki? - Are you okay?

31
02:01.180 --> 02:03.420
What's wrong?

32
02:07.370 --> 02:09.000
Ms. Nashiki?

33
02:09.000 --> 02:11.360
What's wrong?

34
02:11.360 --> 02:12.730
You should go to the nurse.

35
02:12.730 --> 02:15.120
No, I'm fine. I'm fine.

36
02:15.120 --> 02:16.540
You all keep practicing.

37
02:16.540 --> 02:18.150
Ms. Nashiki, you're acting strange.

38
02:18.150 --> 02:20.990
It's like you're back to the old Ms. Nashiki.

39
02:20.990 --> 02:24.710
You're not loud like you usually are.

40
02:24.710 --> 02:30.010
- Yeah. - I liked the loud Ms. Nashiki.

41
02:33.870 --> 02:35.590
I don't remember.

42
02:35.590 --> 02:37.770
I don't remember anything.

43
02:37.770 --> 02:39.420
What have I been doing?

44
02:39.420 --> 02:41.720
Where was I yesterday? The day before?

45
02:41.720 --> 02:45.030
Ms. Nashiki! Good afternoon.

46
02:45.030 --> 02:50.380
Will your class be using this map of Japan?

47
02:50.380 --> 02:53.210
If not, I'll put it away.

48
02:53.210 --> 02:55.810
Mr. Majima.

49
02:56.360 --> 02:57.610
May I ask a question?

50
02:57.610 --> 03:00.070
Of course. What's up?

51
03:00.070 --> 03:02.570
Have I been coming to school?

52
03:02.570 --> 03:04.870
Huh? What do you mean?

53
03:04.870 --> 03:09.780
This entire month, have I...

54
03:09.780 --> 03:12.470
Of course you have.

55
03:17.210 --> 03:19.230
Is everything okay? You seem fatigued.

56
03:19.230 --> 03:21.250
I'm sorry, it's just...

57
03:23.300 --> 03:29.840
How have I been acting this month?

58
03:30.430 --> 03:32.460
How you've been acting? Well...

59
03:38.830 --> 03:43.100
You've certainly become more frank.

60
03:43.100 --> 03:48.110
I can tell you're honest with your students.

61
03:48.110 --> 03:52.410
These days, it feels like...

62
03:53.280 --> 03:56.150
You've really got yourself together.

63
03:59.490 --> 04:02.340
Your whole vibe has changed, too.

64
04:02.340 --> 04:05.190
Did you recharge your batteries over Golden Week?

65
04:05.920 --> 04:08.860
Who is he talking about?

66
04:08.860 --> 04:12.370
I knew it. How, a vacation?

67
04:12.370 --> 04:15.110
I'm sorry. I still have work to finish.

68
04:15.110 --> 04:18.050
Oh, right. See you around.

69
04:22.850 --> 04:25.420
What happened to me?

70
04:25.420 --> 04:27.590
Why can't I remember?

71
04:53.670 --> 04:56.240
[There are two chickens in the garden]

72
05:03.980 --> 05:05.100
Something like that.

73
05:05.100 --> 05:07.600
Saya, you're amazing!

74
05:07.600 --> 05:09.680
You could become a ninja!

75
05:09.680 --> 05:10.980
I'm not doing anything special.

76
05:10.980 --> 05:13.510
- I'm serious. - Okay, your turn.

77
05:14.900 --> 05:20.450
I still don't get it. Why do these give the same character?

78
05:20.450 --> 05:23.280
Why are there two different inputs?

79
05:23.280 --> 05:25.010
Is there an important difference?

80
05:25.010 --> 05:27.640
- No. - What?

81
05:27.640 --> 05:29.740
Just don't question it.

82
05:29.740 --> 05:31.680
- Don't think, feel. - Huh?

83
05:31.680 --> 05:34.220
That's the way it goes.

84
05:34.220 --> 05:36.000
I don't understand.

85
05:36.000 --> 05:39.070
Third graders nowadays can all blind-type.

86
05:39.070 --> 05:40.600
So no complaining, and get typing.

87
05:40.600 --> 05:41.780
- Yes, ma'am! - Alright.

88
05:41.780 --> 05:42.860
- Ready? - Bring it.

89
05:42.860 --> 05:44.080
Go. [Start]

90
05:47.100 --> 05:50.010
Your left hand. Left!

91
05:50.010 --> 05:52.140
Yeah, exactly!

92
05:52.140 --> 05:53.180
You're so slow!

93
05:53.180 --> 05:56.010
Ms. Nashiki, mind if we talk? It's about school.

94
05:56.010 --> 05:58.030
Sure thing.

95
05:58.030 --> 06:00.110
Sorry, I'll be right back.

96
06:00.110 --> 06:02.400
I promise I'll do that later.

97
06:02.400 --> 06:04.540
Just give us a minute.

98
06:09.170 --> 06:11.590
Am I managing to act normal?

99
06:12.260 --> 06:13.060
Yeah.

100
06:13.060 --> 06:15.780
Ms. Nashiki! Ms. Nashiki!

101
06:17.180 --> 06:19.090
Excuse the question, but...

102
06:19.090 --> 06:21.890
Which one are you right now?

103
06:21.890 --> 06:23.310
Which one?

104
06:23.310 --> 06:24.690
What's one plus one?

105
06:24.690 --> 06:27.050
- Two. - No, that doesn't prove anything.

106
06:27.940 --> 06:30.810
Tell me something only a person from Edo would know.

107
06:33.420 --> 06:37.990
Us couriers were sometimes called the Seventeenths.

108
06:40.490 --> 06:42.900
In any case, now we can be certain.

109
06:42.900 --> 06:44.960
- Ms. Nashiki wasn't dead. - Yeah.

110
06:44.960 --> 06:47.690
Her consciousness was just asleep.

111
06:47.690 --> 06:53.550
In other words, if I leave this body, Ms. Nashiki goes back to normal.

112
06:55.270 --> 06:57.900
Damn it all...

113
06:57.900 --> 07:01.660
I really do seem like an evil spirit.

114
07:01.660 --> 07:02.970
That's putting it lightly.

115
07:02.970 --> 07:08.020
Don't laugh. I bet everyone back home is just as worried about me.

116
07:08.020 --> 07:10.150
I've got to get back soon.

117
07:10.780 --> 07:13.250
Yeah.

118
07:18.530 --> 07:20.150
On my bed?

119
07:20.150 --> 07:23.150
How do I get home?

120
07:25.870 --> 07:28.100
Well...

121
07:33.750 --> 07:35.740
The comet.

122
07:35.740 --> 07:37.510
When you first arrived, there was a comet.

123
07:37.510 --> 07:39.940
That one was only once every 341 years,

124
07:39.940 --> 07:42.320
but maybe other astronomical phenomena would do the trick.

125
07:42.320 --> 07:43.580
Astronomical?

126
07:43.580 --> 07:47.400
Meteor showers, eclipses, meteorites - we have several possibilities.

127
07:47.400 --> 07:50.070
Meteorites, meteorites...

128
07:50.070 --> 07:56.020
So you're saying if I'm on that rooftop when one happens, I go home?

129
07:56.020 --> 07:57.610
Exactly!

130
07:58.540 --> 08:00.350
At least, I think so.

131
08:00.350 --> 08:02.620
The location is probably another important factor.

132
08:02.620 --> 08:05.040
That building was nearby Konno Hachimangu.

133
08:05.040 --> 08:08.920
Maybe you were there during the Edo era as well.

134
08:19.880 --> 08:23.510
[Astronomical phenomena - Location] [Connection to Edo]

135
08:23.510 --> 08:26.100
Connected, how? Item...

136
08:26.100 --> 08:29.180
[An item]

137
08:32.170 --> 08:36.210
Have you managed to solve Master Seki's question?

138
08:37.860 --> 08:39.610
Not yet.

139
08:39.610 --> 08:41.960
I'm nowhere close to figuring it out.

140
08:45.610 --> 08:49.050
But I will solve his question.

141
08:50.540 --> 08:52.050
- Still... - Still...

142
08:53.440 --> 08:55.080
You first.

143
08:55.080 --> 08:58.870
Ms. Nashiki tried to die.

144
08:58.870 --> 09:03.490
Yes, and we have to figure out why. Otherwise she might...

145
09:03.490 --> 09:04.950
We can't just "figure it out".

146
09:04.950 --> 09:09.010
Ms. Nashiki has to want to live of her own accord.

147
09:09.010 --> 09:12.220
I can't go back without knowing she's alright.

148
09:16.640 --> 09:20.290
First, let's work out what had driven Ms. Nashiki to such extremes.

149
09:20.290 --> 09:21.730
Right.

150
09:22.560 --> 09:24.980
Have you noticed anything that would potentially bother her?

151
09:24.980 --> 09:27.980
Unreasonable parents, kids who don't attend, stuff like that.

152
09:27.980 --> 09:30.850
A kid who doesn't attend...

153
09:30.850 --> 09:32.700
Actually, yeah. There is one kid who never comes in.

154
09:32.700 --> 09:35.230
Azuki Yoshida.

155
09:35.230 --> 09:37.330
Not here today either, huh?

156
09:37.330 --> 09:40.080
How long haven't they been attending?

157
09:40.080 --> 09:43.350
At the very least, I haven't met them yet.

158
09:43.350 --> 09:46.020
That's a problem.

159
09:46.020 --> 09:48.970
Is it?

160
09:48.970 --> 09:53.260
But farmers this time of year need all the help they can get.

161
09:53.260 --> 09:55.820
- Kids sometimes stay back to help, and... - No, no.

162
09:55.820 --> 09:57.480
That's not how it works now.

163
09:57.480 --> 10:00.400
School is mandatory for all kids.

164
10:00.400 --> 10:01.890
But Saya doesn't go to school.

165
10:01.890 --> 10:03.340
Hey!

166
10:08.920 --> 10:15.210
If Saya chooses not to attend, then I respect her choice.

167
10:15.980 --> 10:19.610
School isn't the only option for kids her age.

168
10:20.490 --> 10:23.530
But your students are only third graders.

169
10:23.530 --> 10:27.160
It may not be their choice that they're missing school.

170
10:27.160 --> 10:31.160
Does that mean something happened to them in April?

171
10:31.160 --> 10:35.890
Only the Ms. Nashiki of the 21st century would know.

172
10:35.890 --> 10:38.560
I see.

173
10:39.240 --> 10:43.530
Thanks, Ikuru. I didn't realize there was a real problem.

174
10:44.500 --> 10:50.640
If only I shared memories with Ms. Nashiki.

175
10:50.640 --> 10:53.310
I'd appreciate that, too.

176
10:53.310 --> 10:56.940
21st century Ms. Nashiki clearly didn't trust me.

177
10:56.940 --> 10:59.050
She looked at me like I was vermin.

178
10:59.050 --> 11:00.660
Hey.

179
11:00.660 --> 11:02.250
Is this...

180
11:03.570 --> 11:05.480
Oh, that? That's from when I was younger.

181
11:05.480 --> 11:08.040
It's a picture of me and my mom.

182
11:08.800 --> 11:11.440
But this...

183
11:11.440 --> 11:13.050
The ocean?

184
11:14.690 --> 11:16.460
I knew it.

185
11:16.460 --> 11:19.090
So this is the ocean.

186
11:20.770 --> 11:24.640
I always heard about it from the couriers.

187
11:24.640 --> 11:28.940
The water really does stretch forever!

188
11:29.640 --> 11:33.430
Do you want to go?

189
11:35.000 --> 11:38.750
Nowadays, it's pretty easy to get there.

190
11:38.750 --> 11:40.500
I'll take you sometime.

191
11:43.870 --> 11:45.720
Promise?

192
11:45.720 --> 11:47.150
Promise.

193
11:52.200 --> 11:56.230
Will Ms. Nashiki really...

194
12:00.160 --> 12:02.420
[Perseids Meteor Shower, August 13th]

195
12:05.300 --> 12:08.230
If she's not able to go home...

196
12:14.780 --> 12:18.180
She'd stay here forever?

197
12:23.760 --> 12:26.730
[World Grand Prix of Poker]

198
12:26.730 --> 12:31.900
At long last, the WGOP has finally begun.

199
12:31.900 --> 12:36.610
One of Japan's very own young stars is testing her skills here today.

200
12:36.610 --> 12:41.840
What I really want isn't something that can be bought with money.

201
12:41.840 --> 12:47.990
So I'll make it my own, using nothing but my own two hands.

202
12:57.910 --> 12:59.450
Ms. Iroha.

203
12:59.990 --> 13:03.040
I don't know a thing about you.

204
13:04.290 --> 13:09.440
But I can tell you were working hard every day.

205
13:11.270 --> 13:16.080
Because these notes, they only mention the good.

206
13:17.360 --> 13:19.620
They make no note of the bad.

207
13:19.620 --> 13:21.730
Or of what hurt you.

208
13:22.950 --> 13:26.170
You weren't writing down the truth.

209
13:27.450 --> 13:31.500
Were you trying to lie, even to your own heart?

210
13:51.280 --> 13:54.690
[Dear Ms. Iroha Nashiki]

211
14:05.010 --> 14:07.230
Morning!

212
14:07.230 --> 14:09.530
Cute!

213
14:09.530 --> 14:11.600
I've never seen that sticker before!

214
14:11.600 --> 14:12.590
Let's trade!

215
14:12.590 --> 14:16.990
But this sticker is super rare.

216
14:17.650 --> 14:22.890
Okay, then I'll trade your Mametchi, for this one!

217
14:22.890 --> 14:26.420
That one is so small.

218
14:27.310 --> 14:29.280
Fine, I'll trade two for that one.

219
14:29.280 --> 14:30.500
Okay!

220
14:31.080 --> 14:32.440
Here.

221
14:36.500 --> 14:38.570
Midori, do you also wanna trade?

222
14:38.570 --> 14:39.980
Yeah.

223
14:41.610 --> 14:43.830
Hey, your stickers aren't puffy.

224
14:43.830 --> 14:45.920
Normal stickers aren't worth much.

225
14:45.920 --> 14:46.940
Yeah.

226
14:46.940 --> 14:50.170
But I feel bad not trading.

227
14:50.170 --> 14:55.300
Here, you can have this Miraitchi if I can have that entire sheet.

228
14:55.300 --> 14:57.840
- The whole thing? - Yeah, you only have normal stickers.

229
14:57.840 --> 15:00.790
Puffy stickers are worth way more.

230
15:00.790 --> 15:03.780
You didn't know, Midori?

231
15:04.540 --> 15:05.990
Here.

232
15:08.570 --> 15:09.910
Lucky!

233
15:09.910 --> 15:11.880
You're so nice, Ichika.

234
15:11.880 --> 15:15.240
I'll always trade with a friend.

235
15:15.240 --> 15:16.980
Thanks.

236
15:21.430 --> 15:23.400
- Look at this one. - Cute!

237
15:23.400 --> 15:24.950
It was the last one.

238
15:24.950 --> 15:26.270
Seriously?

239
15:26.270 --> 15:27.650
I waited three and a half hours for it.

240
15:27.650 --> 15:29.300
No way.

241
15:29.300 --> 15:33.580
Now then, only one month remains until the Sports Festival.

242
15:33.580 --> 15:37.170
I hope preparations are going smoothly for each grade.

243
15:37.170 --> 15:42.170
A representative from the Ministry will come to observe, so please be aware.

244
15:42.170 --> 15:45.720
The Ministry is coming to observe?

245
15:45.720 --> 15:47.010
But why our school?

246
15:47.010 --> 15:51.190
That is because I am the principal here.

247
15:51.190 --> 15:54.260
Only 25% of schools in Japan are led by women.

248
15:54.260 --> 15:56.920
If I am able to be a shining example,

249
15:56.920 --> 16:00.860
it will encourage other women to aim for managerial positions.

250
16:04.290 --> 16:05.980
Inspiring words, ma'am.

251
16:05.980 --> 16:08.080
But the Principal isn't married, is she?

252
16:08.080 --> 16:10.540
Personally, I plan to marry, and have kids.

253
16:10.540 --> 16:12.960
I'm counting on my kids to care for me at her age.

254
16:12.960 --> 16:15.000
- Yikes. - To really make us shine,

255
16:15.000 --> 16:19.280
all faculty will be performing the Soran Bushi sea shanty

256
16:19.280 --> 16:22.450
alongside our sixth graders.

257
16:22.450 --> 16:25.190
I'm counting on you all to get practicing!

258
16:26.270 --> 16:29.290
Come on, let's get pumped, folks!

259
16:29.290 --> 16:30.380
Repeat after me.

260
16:30.380 --> 16:32.940
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

261
16:32.940 --> 16:34.920
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

262
16:34.920 --> 16:36.610
Soran, soran!

263
16:36.610 --> 16:37.920
Soran, soran!

264
16:37.920 --> 16:39.650
Excuse me.

265
16:39.650 --> 16:41.380
Yes, Kamiya?

266
16:41.380 --> 16:44.350
I believe mandatory participation is a form of workplace harassment.

267
16:44.350 --> 16:47.440
No, no. This is no harassment.

268
16:47.440 --> 16:49.130
This is for the Sports Festival!

269
16:49.130 --> 16:55.520
It is an activity for us faculty!

270
16:55.520 --> 16:56.650
Right?

271
16:56.650 --> 16:59.440
- Right, Ms. Nashiki? - Huh? Well...

272
17:00.120 --> 17:03.780
- Yes, Soran. - Ma'am, what's a "soran"?

273
17:03.780 --> 17:07.160
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

274
17:07.160 --> 17:11.040
- Soran, soran! - Oh, like a festival dance?

275
17:11.040 --> 17:15.240
- Seems like fun. - Right, fun! Very fun!

276
17:15.240 --> 17:20.590
We'll hold a kickoff party this Friday for all faculty.

277
17:20.590 --> 17:22.210
Yes, ma'am!

278
17:22.210 --> 17:24.430
Soran, soran!

279
17:24.430 --> 17:27.830
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

280
17:27.830 --> 17:29.910
Soran, soran!

281
17:29.910 --> 17:32.700
Why do we have to do the Soran, too?

282
17:32.700 --> 17:34.600
Yeah...

283
17:34.600 --> 17:37.530
We're already busy with the third grade self-produced dance.

284
17:37.530 --> 17:40.050
Self-produced dance?

285
17:41.880 --> 17:44.680
Listen up, everyone.

286
17:44.680 --> 17:49.170
Since I'm not too good with these tablets, I called Mr. Majima to help out.

287
17:49.170 --> 17:50.900
Mr. Majima, if you'd please.

288
17:50.900 --> 17:52.270
Right.

289
17:52.270 --> 17:54.410
First, I want everyone to find a dance

290
17:54.410 --> 17:58.260
that's trending on Instagram, or Youtube.

291
17:58.260 --> 18:02.010
I'll give you all 10 minutes to search.

292
18:02.010 --> 18:05.280
Ready? Begin.

293
18:05.280 --> 18:06.910
Thank you for helping.

294
18:06.910 --> 18:08.830
Don't thank me just yet.

295
18:08.830 --> 18:12.080
Letting them search freely is the difficult part.

296
18:12.080 --> 18:14.340
Mr. Majima, how should we search?

297
18:14.340 --> 18:15.480
Good question.

298
18:15.480 --> 18:18.780
First, practice typing in some keywords

299
18:18.780 --> 18:21.740
for what you're looking for.

300
18:21.740 --> 18:24.390
For example, "Sports Festival Dance",

301
18:24.390 --> 18:27.340
or "Third Grader Tries to Dance".

302
18:27.340 --> 18:30.290
Try these words out, and see what you find.

303
18:30.290 --> 18:31.380
[TubeKing]

304
18:31.380 --> 18:35.710
When you find something interesting, send the URL here.

305
19:00.730 --> 19:02.880
What're you looking at, Midori?

306
19:04.220 --> 19:07.160
Those are some pretty stones.

307
19:07.160 --> 19:09.630
No looking up anything irrelevant.

308
19:09.630 --> 19:12.460
You all have eight minutes left.

309
19:18.290 --> 19:20.630
All students in attendance sent their URLs,

310
19:20.630 --> 19:23.220
so I'll sort them alongside my class.

311
19:23.220 --> 19:25.320
Thank you.

312
19:25.320 --> 19:28.060
Mr. Majima.

313
19:28.060 --> 19:30.040
You were so deft.

314
19:30.040 --> 19:32.290
- Almost like a ninja. - Huh?

315
19:32.290 --> 19:34.390
A ninja?

316
19:34.390 --> 19:37.540
You're able to type on that tablet,

317
19:37.540 --> 19:42.100
all while instructing the kids.

318
19:42.100 --> 19:47.270
Almost made me want to pay you.

319
19:47.270 --> 19:49.350
You really are strange, Ms. Nashiki.

320
19:49.350 --> 19:52.540
- Hey! No running in the halls! - Yes, Ms. Nashiki.

321
19:52.540 --> 19:58.640
I've never met someone who didn't know about YouTube or Instagram before.

322
19:58.640 --> 20:00.540
Sorry, I'll study up on them.

323
20:00.540 --> 20:04.540
No, I'm not saying that's a bad thing.

324
20:04.540 --> 20:08.220
If anything, it's nice.

325
20:08.220 --> 20:09.270
Huh?

326
20:09.270 --> 20:11.580
Oh, never mind.

327
20:11.580 --> 20:13.600
Let's get to our classes.

328
20:14.480 --> 20:17.540
One more thing, Mr. Majima.

329
20:17.540 --> 20:21.540
I need to talk to you about something.

330
20:24.250 --> 20:27.010
I'll meet you on the roof after school.

331
20:27.010 --> 20:28.390
- Let's go! - Yeah!

332
20:28.390 --> 20:32.050
Hey! I said no running!

333
20:35.630 --> 20:37.020
Okay!

334
20:40.160 --> 20:42.670
Wrong way.

335
20:42.670 --> 20:46.310
Midori. You were looking up stickers earlier, weren't you?

336
20:46.310 --> 20:47.760
No.

337
20:47.760 --> 20:49.140
Didn't you know?

338
20:49.140 --> 20:53.040
Stickers sold online are all fake.

339
20:53.040 --> 20:56.830
No one will trade for fakes.

340
20:56.830 --> 20:59.000
Get your mom to buy you some!

341
20:59.000 --> 21:01.300
Ichika, let's go.

342
21:01.300 --> 21:02.720
Yeah.

343
21:02.720 --> 21:04.490
Come on.

344
21:04.490 --> 21:07.300
Let's trade more stickers later!

345
21:26.680 --> 21:28.030
Mr. Majima.

346
21:28.030 --> 21:29.930
Have all your students gone home?

347
21:31.050 --> 21:31.790
Yeah.

348
21:31.790 --> 21:34.740
The third and fourth grade teachers have to settle details for the relay race.

349
21:34.740 --> 21:39.230
Sorry, I have something to attend to first.

350
22:14.760 --> 22:16.200
Mr. Majima.

351
22:16.200 --> 22:18.460
Thanks for coming, I know you're busy.

352
22:18.460 --> 22:20.100
No, it's fine.

353
22:20.680 --> 22:22.210
So...

354
22:23.920 --> 22:26.570
What is it you wished to talk about?

355
22:26.570 --> 22:28.090
Well...

356
22:29.210 --> 22:32.490
How to put it...

357
22:38.170 --> 22:44.710
It seems acting normal at school is advised.

358
22:45.380 --> 22:48.540
Only the Principal needs to be informed.

359
22:48.540 --> 22:53.690
Then one or the other will be transferred to another school.

360
22:54.240 --> 22:56.120
What are you talking about?

361
22:57.020 --> 23:02.190
I was only giving an example of what could happen.

362
23:02.190 --> 23:04.970
What I wanted to ask you...

363
23:06.080 --> 23:10.770
Is what I was like in April.

364
23:10.770 --> 23:13.520
Huh? What you were like in April?

365
23:13.520 --> 23:15.950
Yeah. Did I cause any trouble?

366
23:15.950 --> 23:18.770
Why are you asking me? You would know best, right?

367
23:18.770 --> 23:22.300
Actually, I can't seem to remember.

368
23:22.300 --> 23:24.080
What?

369
23:24.080 --> 23:25.950
You don't remember?

370
23:29.340 --> 23:31.310
No wonder you said that the other day.

371
23:31.310 --> 23:32.880
Said, what?

372
23:32.880 --> 23:36.970
You asked if you were coming to school.

373
23:42.970 --> 23:45.440
Sorry for asking something so weird.

374
23:53.860 --> 23:56.650
Where did you go on vacation over Golden Week?

375
23:56.650 --> 23:59.320
Vacation?

376
23:59.320 --> 24:03.420
Wherever you went completely changed you.

377
24:04.640 --> 24:06.130
No, I...

378
24:07.030 --> 24:11.560
I like it here.

379
24:14.210 --> 24:17.640
I always wanted to become a teacher.

380
24:17.640 --> 24:21.360
It was something I thought I could only dream of.

381
24:22.940 --> 24:25.840
So this is already the place of my dreams.

382
24:27.350 --> 24:31.440
I wanted to become a teacher, and now I am.

383
24:31.440 --> 24:34.490
I couldn't ask for anything more.

384
24:38.320 --> 24:40.020
I see.

385
24:40.910 --> 24:45.150
So you must have remembered why you became a teacher in the first place.

386
24:47.570 --> 24:53.020
I actually did my student teaching at the elementary school I attended.

387
24:53.020 --> 24:56.580
At the time, I marveled at how small the tables were,

388
24:56.580 --> 24:58.310
how perfect teachers were, and...

389
24:58.310 --> 25:00.180
Mr. Majima.

390
25:00.180 --> 25:01.470
Yes?

391
25:01.470 --> 25:05.640
One of my students isn't attending school.

392
25:05.640 --> 25:07.380
Oh...

393
25:07.380 --> 25:09.620
The kid who stopped coming at the end of April?

394
25:09.620 --> 25:11.580
Yes, them.

395
25:12.470 --> 25:16.960
Some kids tend to burn out in April.

396
25:16.960 --> 25:20.330
Just give them time. It'll be fine.

397
25:20.330 --> 25:22.050
I see.

398
25:24.840 --> 25:28.160
Gosh, I can't help it.

399
25:28.160 --> 25:30.920
I keep relying on you, don't I?

400
25:30.920 --> 25:33.000
Thank you, Mr. Majima.

401
25:36.300 --> 25:38.650
Ms. Nashiki.

402
25:38.650 --> 25:39.980
Yes?

403
25:43.080 --> 25:48.170
Would you like to get dinner together sometime?

404
25:48.170 --> 25:49.980
Together?

405
25:56.880 --> 25:58.420
Sorry for interrupting.

406
25:58.420 --> 26:00.870
I wonder who left these buckets here.

407
26:00.870 --> 26:02.920
What are you doing here, Mr. Ichinose?

408
26:02.920 --> 26:05.900
Well, you know.

409
26:08.440 --> 26:10.740
I came to see the blue skies.

410
26:10.740 --> 26:12.530
It's cloudy.

411
26:12.530 --> 26:15.180
If it's dinner you're asking about, there's the faculty party this Friday.

412
26:15.180 --> 26:18.850
Great timing, right? Great timing indeed.

413
26:18.850 --> 26:20.540
Mr. Ichinose.

414
26:20.540 --> 26:24.920
You and Ms. Nashiki have been quite close recently.

415
26:24.920 --> 26:25.730
No.

416
26:25.730 --> 26:30.150
Pardon me for asking, but are you two...

417
26:31.310 --> 26:32.680
In a relationship?

418
26:32.680 --> 26:36.720
No, no! Of course not!

419
26:36.720 --> 26:38.020
Right, Ms. Nashiki?

420
26:38.020 --> 26:41.130
Yeah. I just stay with Ikuru.

421
26:41.130 --> 26:42.710
Huh? Stay with him?

422
26:42.710 --> 26:44.580
No, no!

423
26:44.580 --> 26:47.900
She meant to say, uh, smile with him!

424
26:47.900 --> 26:49.880
The hell do you mean, smile?

425
26:49.880 --> 26:53.350
Ms. Nashiki, we need you. Come with me!

426
26:53.350 --> 26:54.870
- What now? - Excuse us!

427
26:54.870 --> 26:56.960
Hey!

428
26:59.040 --> 27:02.050
"Ikuru", is it.

429
27:03.020 --> 27:04.610
That scared me.

430
27:05.960 --> 27:07.130
Why'd you run away?

431
27:07.130 --> 27:09.720
I couldn't help it!

432
27:09.720 --> 27:11.160
Excuse us.

433
27:16.290 --> 27:19.670
Right. I asked around about Ms. Nashiki.

434
27:19.670 --> 27:25.090
Apparently, she barely spoke to our other staff in April.

435
27:25.090 --> 27:27.980
Ms. Nashiki?

436
27:29.300 --> 27:33.180
Well, we tried making conversation with her.

437
27:33.180 --> 27:35.240
Yeah, she seemed to be on edge all the time.

438
27:35.240 --> 27:38.990
We'd advise her to relax, and loosen up.

439
27:38.990 --> 27:42.960
But we didn't want to make it seem like we were cautioning her.

440
27:42.960 --> 27:45.240
- I didn't want to be accused of harassment. - Right.

441
27:45.240 --> 27:49.660
But part of teaching is dealing with the unreasonable.

442
27:49.660 --> 27:51.760
Well, that's another issue entirely.

443
27:51.760 --> 27:54.970
Ms. Nashiki had just returned from a year long break from work.

444
27:54.970 --> 28:00.100
She may have been worried about the impression she left others.

445
28:04.320 --> 28:06.870
That must have been rough.

446
28:06.870 --> 28:09.770
I wonder if she had anyone to confide in...

447
28:10.960 --> 28:12.630
What about you, Ikuru?

448
28:13.570 --> 28:14.530
Huh?

449
28:14.530 --> 28:17.430
Were you close with Ms. Nashiki?

450
28:19.510 --> 28:20.830
No.

451
28:28.850 --> 28:30.380
What's wrong?

452
28:31.860 --> 28:33.110
Nothing.

453
28:33.110 --> 28:34.770
- Let's get back to work. - Yeah.

454
28:34.770 --> 28:36.130
You move.

455
28:36.130 --> 28:37.570
- I can't. - Stop kicking me.

456
28:37.570 --> 28:40.470
No fighting, you two.

457
28:44.960 --> 28:47.980
[S-Ward School's third grade teacher wasn't working last year. Yikes!]

458
28:54.490 --> 28:57.970
[Class 3 Moms' Group Chat]

459
29:01.510 --> 29:03.300
[Did you hear?]

460
29:03.300 --> 29:05.350
[Ms. Nashiki hasn't confiscated sticker albums from her students]

461
29:05.350 --> 29:07.620
[Really?] [But toys aren't allowed in school]

462
29:07.620 --> 29:10.710
[She needs to reassess her responsibilities] Mom, I'm hungry.

463
29:11.330 --> 29:13.350
Mom?

464
29:13.350 --> 29:16.850
Does everyone have their drinks?

465
29:16.850 --> 29:18.530
- Yes. - Yup.

466
29:18.530 --> 29:23.750
Here's to our upcoming Sports Festival!

467
29:23.750 --> 29:24.910
Cheers!

468
29:24.910 --> 29:28.230
Cheers!

469
29:29.840 --> 29:35.180
We're also celebrating our two new hires so let loose, and no holding back!

470
29:35.180 --> 29:38.550
- Thank you. - Thank you!

471
29:42.030 --> 29:44.100
Ms. President, allow me to pour you a glass.

472
29:44.100 --> 29:48.910
Ichinose, I can tell you're a rookie.

473
29:48.910 --> 29:50.130
How so?

474
29:50.130 --> 29:53.770
At these sorts of functions, we call the Principal, "President".

475
29:53.770 --> 29:56.320
- President? - The Head of Year is your "Manager".

476
29:56.320 --> 29:58.860
We never know when parents are listening, after all.

477
29:58.860 --> 30:03.100
- I see. - Walls always have ears.

478
30:03.100 --> 30:04.920
And parents are hidden in the masses.

479
30:04.920 --> 30:06.500
I appreciate the advice.

480
30:06.500 --> 30:09.610
That makes parents ninjas, too.

481
30:09.610 --> 30:13.210
Huh? You're both drinking tea?

482
30:13.210 --> 30:15.050
Yes. I won't be drinking alcohol today.

483
30:15.050 --> 30:19.000
Oh, come on. If you can drink, drink!

484
30:19.000 --> 30:20.520
As I said, let loose.

485
30:20.520 --> 30:23.980
Treat this party like an icebreaker!

486
30:24.500 --> 30:26.970
No, Ms. Akutsu...

487
30:37.850 --> 30:39.520
Thank you.

488
30:45.700 --> 30:48.470
The hell is this?

489
30:48.470 --> 30:52.810
It's yellow, but it's a fine brew!

490
30:52.810 --> 30:54.500
That's a western alcoholic drink.

491
30:54.500 --> 30:56.920
Western alcohol?

492
30:56.920 --> 30:59.480
Westerners know their stuff!

493
30:59.480 --> 31:03.060
Has she never had beer before?

494
31:03.060 --> 31:05.560
Or are you more a fan of Japanese sake?

495
31:06.120 --> 31:08.240
I think there was some on the menu...

496
31:08.240 --> 31:10.950
Nah, I like this stuff.

497
31:10.950 --> 31:12.530
May I have another glass?

498
31:14.390 --> 31:16.010
Thank you.

499
31:19.880 --> 31:21.310
I feel my throat pricking!

500
31:21.310 --> 31:22.320
We call that "sparkling".

501
31:22.320 --> 31:23.580
And this bitterness is divine!

502
31:23.580 --> 31:24.560
That's the hops.

503
31:24.560 --> 31:25.890
And these bubbles...

504
31:25.890 --> 31:28.190
You've got some there! Avoid that, it's seen as cunning.

505
31:28.190 --> 31:30.240
- Huh? - There, above your lip.

506
31:30.240 --> 31:33.160
Now hold on just a second.

507
31:33.160 --> 31:36.230
- Yes? - You two seem close.

508
31:36.230 --> 31:37.570
Huh?

509
31:37.570 --> 31:39.110
No, no.

510
31:39.110 --> 31:45.390
Oh? Already? Am I going to have to do it?

511
31:45.390 --> 31:48.600
Am I sending one of you away next year?

512
31:48.600 --> 31:49.910
- Sorry! - Hey!

513
31:49.910 --> 31:52.320
So sorry! The plates are safe.

514
31:52.320 --> 31:54.740
Who cares about the damn plates.

515
31:55.650 --> 31:58.890
You almost got jijimi sauce on Rinma.

516
31:58.890 --> 32:00.360
Rinma?

517
32:01.650 --> 32:06.110
Oh, that jerk from "Mr. Butler"? Think I've seen him around...

518
32:11.810 --> 32:14.050
- Say that again. - Huh?

519
32:14.980 --> 32:17.060
Surely I was just hearing things, right?

520
32:17.060 --> 32:20.430
Surely you didn't disrespect his name.

521
32:20.430 --> 32:22.490
Huh? No, I...

522
32:23.660 --> 32:27.000
Rinma Endo has a name.

523
32:27.810 --> 32:30.080
So use it.

524
32:30.080 --> 32:35.170
Mr. Rinma Endo.

525
32:35.690 --> 32:37.180
Thank you.

526
32:42.420 --> 32:46.490
It was far too early to turn you to ashes...

527
32:46.490 --> 32:48.000
Help, she's scaring me!

528
32:48.000 --> 32:52.050
Gosh, I'm glad our teachers are looking out for each other.

529
32:52.050 --> 32:53.320
- How? - And you're wrong!

530
32:53.320 --> 32:55.740
Then let me ask the group.

531
32:55.740 --> 33:02.400
Who here... has kissed in a classroom!

532
33:02.400 --> 33:04.370
Ms. Principal!

533
33:04.370 --> 33:07.320
We're breaking ice!

534
33:07.320 --> 33:10.270
Come on, be honest!

535
33:10.270 --> 33:13.980
Anyone? Anyone?

536
33:16.700 --> 33:20.910
Could we get another order of chilled tomatoes?

537
33:20.910 --> 33:22.980
Chilled tomatoes, coming right up!

538
33:23.900 --> 33:26.130
- Would you all like some, too? - Yes, please!

539
33:26.130 --> 33:28.570
- Please make that three chilled tomatoes! - Sure thing!

540
33:36.610 --> 33:39.600
Here are your chilled tomatoes.

541
33:39.600 --> 33:41.700
Hey!

542
33:41.700 --> 33:44.250
Eat slower! This isn't our lunch break!

543
33:44.250 --> 33:46.480
Say what?

544
33:46.480 --> 33:49.880
Eating fast is ingrained in us teachers.

545
33:49.880 --> 33:52.990
Really, we should be getting paid for attending this party.

546
33:52.990 --> 33:54.810
Two more samgyeopsal's, please.

547
33:54.810 --> 33:56.740
If you're only going to complain, don't come.

548
33:56.740 --> 33:58.360
I'd be told off if I didn't.

549
33:58.360 --> 33:59.530
That's also harassment.

550
33:59.530 --> 34:04.040
Calling everything harassment is also a form of harassment.

551
34:04.040 --> 34:06.350
- Exactly. - Mr. Konishi.

552
34:06.350 --> 34:09.020
How'd it go with the dating app girl?

553
34:09.020 --> 34:13.870
Hear this. I had to stay after school, and was late to one date,

554
34:13.870 --> 34:16.020
and she called our whole relationship off!

555
34:16.020 --> 34:17.090
What?

556
34:17.090 --> 34:20.210
Your sake.

557
34:20.210 --> 34:21.450
Sake!

558
34:21.450 --> 34:24.790
Stop, you've already reached your limit.

559
34:24.790 --> 34:26.480
You've drunk far too much.

560
34:26.480 --> 34:28.500
Hey!

561
34:28.500 --> 34:31.970
I know that thing! On your tag, there.

562
34:31.970 --> 34:34.940
I saw it earlier today. Such a doll!

563
34:34.940 --> 34:37.200
- A doll... - Sorry about her.

564
34:37.200 --> 34:38.910
She means it's cute.

565
34:38.910 --> 34:41.420
Stickers, huh?

566
34:41.420 --> 34:43.600
I confiscated another binder today.

567
34:43.600 --> 34:48.100
Same. I have to remind my students not to bring them every day.

568
34:48.100 --> 34:50.440
They're not allowed to bring them?

569
34:50.440 --> 34:51.610
Why not?

570
34:51.610 --> 34:53.280
Isn't that obvious?

571
34:53.280 --> 34:56.760
If we allowed it, there'd be a divide between kids with stickers and without.

572
34:56.760 --> 35:00.480
Yeah. They'd start fighting, saying it's unfair and all.

573
35:00.480 --> 35:02.260
Why?

574
35:02.260 --> 35:06.980
Let's say there's a kid with tons of stickers.

575
35:06.980 --> 35:10.380
Seeing this, another kid is sad they have none.

576
35:10.380 --> 35:12.480
If they're not all equal, that's just unfair.

577
35:12.480 --> 35:14.220
Unfair?

578
35:14.940 --> 35:19.470
Elementary school is a place where we aim for all kids to be equal.

579
35:19.470 --> 35:22.790
It's also so our kids maintain their self-esteem.

580
35:22.790 --> 35:25.550
Encouraging inequality does no one any good.

581
35:25.550 --> 35:27.090
Exactly.

582
35:29.360 --> 35:35.670
But what does equality really mean?

583
35:35.670 --> 35:36.890
Huh?

584
35:36.890 --> 35:40.730
I mean, this world is plenty unequal, right?

585
35:40.730 --> 35:42.430
Ms. Nashiki, that's no way to...

586
35:42.430 --> 35:44.250
- Ms. Principal. - President.

587
35:44.250 --> 35:47.560
You agree with me, right?

588
35:47.560 --> 35:50.190
This world ain't equal.

589
35:50.190 --> 35:54.260
The child of the shogun and the child of a peasant are different.

590
35:54.260 --> 35:56.620
Peasant?

591
35:56.620 --> 35:57.820
I see...

592
35:57.820 --> 35:59.640
Maybe ages ago, but...

593
35:59.640 --> 36:03.280
The child of a merchant wears a quality kimono.

594
36:03.280 --> 36:07.890
While farming children are barefoot even in the winter. That's a given.

595
36:07.890 --> 36:10.420
It's how things are.

596
36:10.420 --> 36:12.940
- Ms. Nashiki, please stop. - I'm not wrong, am I?

597
36:12.940 --> 36:14.070
Right, sorry.

598
36:14.070 --> 36:16.500
And the child of a courier

599
36:16.500 --> 36:20.550
has their own life to live.

600
36:21.960 --> 36:24.250
No amount of complaining will change that.

601
36:24.250 --> 36:28.210
They feel it's unfair to be compared to other kids?

602
36:28.210 --> 36:33.380
Then they oughta live the life befitting their standing.

603
36:34.800 --> 36:37.630
I understand what you're trying to say.

604
36:37.630 --> 36:40.620
And honestly, you're right.

605
36:40.620 --> 36:47.140
The household you're born in dictates the start you'll get in life.

606
36:47.140 --> 36:48.750
That's the reality of it all.

607
36:48.750 --> 36:51.790
Ms. Principal - I mean, President...

608
36:51.790 --> 36:56.270
But when we teachers strive for equality,

609
36:56.270 --> 37:01.040
we're not necessarily trying to change the way the world works.

610
37:01.040 --> 37:03.940
The way the world works?

611
37:03.940 --> 37:09.840
School is a place where kids spend a majority of their days at.

612
37:09.840 --> 37:13.450
It's a place to nurture their futures.

613
37:13.450 --> 37:21.630
Do you think it's our place to arbitrarily decide who they're meant to be?

614
37:23.500 --> 37:26.390
Add these two horizontal bars,

615
37:26.390 --> 37:30.950
and you get a total of 399.

616
37:32.420 --> 37:33.660
Run.

617
37:33.660 --> 37:35.790
You three.

618
37:36.480 --> 37:38.080
Yes, you three there.

619
37:38.890 --> 37:40.780
Come here.

620
37:40.780 --> 37:42.440
- Should we? - Come.

621
37:42.440 --> 37:44.460
Come here.

622
37:44.460 --> 37:45.940
Don't be shy.

623
37:46.380 --> 37:53.560
♪ Align your calculating sticks, and the path shall open ♪

624
37:53.560 --> 37:56.940
♪ It shall open wide for you ♪

625
37:56.940 --> 38:00.890
♪ Line your horizontals and verticals ♪

626
38:00.890 --> 38:04.450
♪ and you get your number ♪

627
38:04.450 --> 38:08.760
♪ The correct answer ♪

628
38:12.310 --> 38:17.120
To bring it back to stickers, kids with stickers aren't to blame.

629
38:17.120 --> 38:19.700
Neither are those without stickers.

630
38:19.700 --> 38:25.560
But when they're brought into the classroom for all to see...

631
38:26.280 --> 38:30.560
The kids end up ranking themselves.

632
38:30.560 --> 38:34.600
Exactly. Each child mentally starts ranking the others.

633
38:34.600 --> 38:38.150
And we want to prevent that from happening.

634
38:39.510 --> 38:44.080
I do think it's important to live a life appropriate of one's standing.

635
38:44.080 --> 38:50.630
But children know nothing of their own "standing" yet.

636
38:50.630 --> 38:57.970
And school can't be the place where that arbitrary decision is made.

637
38:58.660 --> 39:02.690
It has to remain a place of equality.

638
39:04.310 --> 39:06.140
I see.

639
39:07.020 --> 39:09.120
I understand.

640
39:11.740 --> 39:15.770
Folks, I appreciate your guidance.

641
39:20.200 --> 39:24.290
That was a moving speech.

642
39:24.290 --> 39:26.480
Equal, as all schools should be!

643
39:26.480 --> 39:29.290
That's right. What a riveting ice breaker.

644
39:29.290 --> 39:34.600
Yes! I feel like my speech was very inspiring.

645
39:34.600 --> 39:38.000
Did anyone record that?

646
39:38.000 --> 39:40.110
Me. I'm always recording.

647
39:40.110 --> 39:44.560
I won't dwell on the implications.

648
39:44.560 --> 39:48.280
In any case, rather than apologize,

649
39:48.280 --> 39:51.390
I'd appreciate if you put that effort towards the Soran Bushi.

650
39:51.390 --> 39:53.900
The Soran Bushi...

651
39:53.900 --> 39:56.890
Right, of course! How could I forget?

652
39:56.890 --> 39:58.550
The entertainment!

653
39:58.550 --> 39:59.560
Entertainment?

654
39:59.560 --> 40:03.460
I did plenty of that for the Tokubei gang.

655
40:03.460 --> 40:05.880
Parties need their entertainment!

656
40:05.880 --> 40:08.940
G-Gang?

657
40:09.910 --> 40:13.130
I, Iroha of the Tokubei's, shall now demonstrate!

658
40:15.010 --> 40:16.380
You can't!

659
40:16.380 --> 40:19.780
We must dance!

660
40:19.780 --> 40:21.540
Go, Ms. Nashiki!

661
40:21.540 --> 40:24.830
Heave-ho! Heave-ho!

662
40:24.830 --> 40:27.580
Don't look! No!

663
40:27.580 --> 40:30.750
- Ms. Nashiki! Stop that! - Soran, soran!

664
40:37.120 --> 40:40.450
Where is he? Found him!

665
40:48.940 --> 40:50.690
Ms. Akutsu?

666
40:50.690 --> 40:51.820
Mind if I record?

667
40:51.820 --> 40:54.260
Please don't! Don't!

668
40:54.260 --> 40:57.150
Ms. Nashiki, over here!

669
41:06.470 --> 41:08.030
Ms. Akutsu.

670
41:10.020 --> 41:12.220
Is Ms. Nashiki...

671
41:12.980 --> 41:15.910
the daughter of some gang?

672
41:15.910 --> 41:17.140
Huh?

673
41:17.140 --> 41:21.080
She claimed she was associated with one!

674
41:21.080 --> 41:22.820
Should we not get involved with her?

675
41:22.820 --> 41:24.580
Don't know.

676
41:24.580 --> 41:28.100
But if she is, I'm rooting for her and the young boss.

677
41:28.100 --> 41:30.330
Young boss? Who?

678
41:31.020 --> 41:32.620
You're not making any sense.

679
41:33.890 --> 41:35.540
Wait, you mean...

680
41:38.330 --> 41:40.090
Is that what you mean?

681
41:41.040 --> 41:43.090
Is it?

682
41:46.900 --> 41:49.750
Looks like fireworks out there.

683
41:49.750 --> 41:52.150
Everything's sparkling.

684
41:52.150 --> 41:54.520
I'm not surprised, given how much you drank.

685
41:56.550 --> 41:59.310
Here, have some water.

686
42:07.380 --> 42:10.980
Ms. Nashiki, you can press that button.

687
42:18.690 --> 42:20.310
I can't believe you.

688
42:20.310 --> 42:22.790
No one belly dances like that nowadays.

689
42:22.790 --> 42:24.370
It's unheard of.

690
42:24.370 --> 42:27.180
Who cares? Not like it's doing me harm.

691
42:27.180 --> 42:29.150
It is though!

692
42:29.770 --> 42:31.180
Your skin...

693
42:33.810 --> 42:36.730
It's not something to show others.

694
42:36.730 --> 42:39.960
"Others"?

695
42:39.960 --> 42:43.090
Our coworkers are like family.

696
42:43.090 --> 42:44.640
No, they are not.

697
42:44.640 --> 42:46.620
What are you talking about?

698
42:47.950 --> 42:50.240
You need to be more cautious, Ms. Nashiki.

699
42:50.240 --> 42:53.150
That's why people misunderstand.

700
42:53.150 --> 42:55.410
Misunderstand?

701
42:55.410 --> 42:59.290
Would you like to get dinner together sometime?

702
42:59.290 --> 43:02.000
Dinner?

703
43:03.050 --> 43:07.240
You can't be nice to every last person you meet.

704
43:07.240 --> 43:09.120
Please learn some self-restraint.

705
43:09.120 --> 43:13.900
The hell? You act like I'm a lecher.

706
43:13.900 --> 43:15.980
A lecher?

707
43:15.980 --> 43:17.580
No, I just...

708
43:17.580 --> 43:20.330
I want you to stop acting so carelessly.

709
43:20.330 --> 43:22.290
Why?

710
43:22.290 --> 43:23.950
"Why"?

711
43:29.180 --> 43:33.720
Well... that's because...

712
43:44.450 --> 43:46.970
This is our stop.

713
43:48.380 --> 43:50.490
- Grab your things. - Okay.

714
43:53.990 --> 43:55.610
Ikuru.

715
43:57.230 --> 43:59.000
Rinka?

716
43:59.580 --> 44:01.190
You came back?

717
44:01.190 --> 44:03.160
You didn't check your phone?

718
44:03.160 --> 44:04.610
My phone?

719
44:08.770 --> 44:11.480
Who's this?

720
44:11.480 --> 44:14.530
Oh, uh... this is my coworker.

721
44:14.530 --> 44:16.430
You're heading home with your coworker?

722
44:16.430 --> 44:18.530
That's 'cause we're friends.

723
44:18.530 --> 44:20.030
Right. We're friends.

724
44:20.030 --> 44:23.230
She's my neighbor.

725
44:23.230 --> 44:24.720
I see.

726
44:24.720 --> 44:30.480
If you're Ikuru's friend, I'd like to be friends, too.

727
44:30.480 --> 44:32.850
- What's your name? - Nashiki.

728
44:32.850 --> 44:35.390
Iroha Nashiki.

729
44:35.390 --> 44:37.170
- Iroha. - Yes.

730
44:37.170 --> 44:38.960
Nice to meet you.

731
44:54.790 --> 44:59.080
I'm actually a bit tired today.

732
44:59.830 --> 45:03.220
Iroha. Let's talk again sometime.

733
45:03.220 --> 45:04.270
Yeah.

734
45:04.270 --> 45:06.860
You must be tired from the tournament.

735
45:06.860 --> 45:09.140
- Take care. - Yeah.

736
45:09.140 --> 45:11.290
Ms. Nashiki, not that way.

737
45:11.290 --> 45:13.070
This way.

738
45:13.070 --> 45:17.400
Oh, right. Knowing you, I bet you won. Congrats.

739
45:18.010 --> 45:19.490
See you around.

740
45:19.490 --> 45:21.080
You don't need to copy me.

741
45:21.080 --> 45:22.740
Watch your step.

742
45:22.740 --> 45:24.270
Come on.

743
45:25.530 --> 45:28.060
We're not crossing. This way.
